<title>BELGIUM: EU FAILS TO AGREE ON POSTAL LIBERALISATION.</title>
<headline>EU FAILS TO AGREE ON POSTAL LIBERALISATION.</headline>
<dateline>BRUSSELS 1996-11-28</dateline>
<text>
<p>European Union ministers failed to reach a deal on Thursday on when and how to open EU postal services to competition, EU officials said.</p>
<p>The post and telecommunications ministers were deadlocked on the question of ending the monopolies of state post offices over direct or &quot;junk&quot; mail and cross-border mail.</p>
<p>They were unable to bridge the gap between a Franco-German camp that did not want to set a firm date for opening those sectors to competition and others who wanted to establish a timetable. -- Brussels Newsroom 32 2 287 6800</p>
</text>
